      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GOD'S CHOICE (9) resumed in much stronger company 40 days ago where she was just fair. She's been back to the trials since where she looked good and she has found a suitable race coming back to this level. Looks the one to beat in this. CARTIER GLOW (7) led them up on debut but was caught late over 1000m at Bunbury. This looks a little easier, though there is a query as the trainer did say he was shin sore first-up. He's right in this if he's overcome that niggle. DIP IT IN A DREAM (8) comes through the same trial as Tex 'N' Cee last time and Faithfull reunites with the gelding after being on board with three of his four trials. Won't be far away. SALVE REGINA (5) will appreciate firmer footing this time around and won't be far away. KIAM'S CHOICE (4) can improve in a more suitable race this time.",
